{"name":"Blood Orange","hex":"#d1001c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blood orange","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of orange (a variety of Citrus sinensis) notable for its dark, crimson red flesh."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blood_orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blood Orange (1953 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blood Orange is a 1953 British crime drama directed by Terence Fisher and starring Tom Conway and Mila Parély. The screenplay was by Jan Read. J. Elder Wills was art director, Phil Leakey Makeup, and Jimmy Sangster was assistant director. Filming began on March 16, 1953, and the film was released on Oct. 10, 1953. Most reviewers commented on how uneventful the film was, which is surprising given its extremely complex plot."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/0e/Blood_Orange_film_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_Orange_(1953_film)"},{"title":"Blood Orange (2016 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Blood Orange is a 2016 film noir directed by Toby Tobias and starring Iggy Pop as an ageing rock star (Bill) and Kacey Barnfield as his young wife (Isabelle). It is the first film in which Iggy Pop played a lead role, although he had previously had cameo roles in several films."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_Orange_(2016_film)"},{"title":"Blood orange","blocks":[{"text":"The blood orange is a variety of orange with crimson flesh colored near or the same as blood. It is one of the sweet orange varieties. It is also known as the raspberry orange."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/BloodOrange.jpg/330px-BloodOrange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_orange"},{"title":"Blood","blocks":[{"text":"Blood is a specialized form of connective tissue and body fluid in the circulatory system of humans and other vertebrates that delivers necessary substances such as nutrients and oxygen to the cells of the body, and transports metabolic waste products away from those same cells."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Venous_and_arterial_blood.jpg/330px-Venous_and_arterial_blood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg/500px-Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg/1280px-Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg/500px-Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Immature 'Moro' blood orange fruit – 7 months from flowering","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AImmature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bloodorange1.jpg/500px-Bloodorange1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bloodorange1.jpg/1280px-Bloodorange1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bloodorange1.jpg/500px-Bloodorange1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A glass of Sanguinel